<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alulim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alulim is the first king named in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a>, which states that after kingship descended from heaven it was at Eridu, where Alulim reigned for 28,800 years. He is a legendary figure belonging to the list's mythical era before the flood. His successor at Eridu is given as Alalngar, after which kingship passed to other cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alulim.jpg" alt="Alulim" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lista_Reale_Sumerica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
